The short version
Xano owns the reservation, the money, and whether a unit is available.
Memberstack is login and page gating. Payfast's ITN is the only trustworthy
signal that money moved.
The Webflow CMS stays the catalogue. Units, add-ons and properties are
edited there as they are today; Xano mirrors what it needs to price and lock.
The CMS knows sold and reserved; Xano knows held.
Never rename across a boundary. Webflow form field names, CMS slugs,
Memberstack sub-status values and Payfast field names are all frozen.
Translation happens in field-map.js and nowhere else.
Rules that are easy to get wrong
Money is integer _cents everywhere. Format to two decimals only when
handing an amount to Payfast.
The Payfast amount comes from the CMS (payment-amount on the Reservation
Step 3 collection), read server-side. The request body never carries an
amount.
Rebuild the ITN signature from the raw body in the order received —
parsed input objects don't preserve it.
use-live-payments is per property. A property left on sandbox takes no
real money.
sales_stage values stay kebab-case because they came from Memberstack and
the portal still reads them. Our own statuses are snake_case. This is
deliberate — see the registry.
Keeping these current
These are exports of three artifacts on claude.ai. If you edit here, they're the
source of truth and the artifacts are stale — say so at the top of the file
rather than letting two versions drift, which is the exact failure the naming
registry exists to prevent.
